  "notes": "{憎|にく}い has two distinct uses. The primary meaning expresses genuine hatred or detestation. The secondary meaning is ironic praise — expressing grudging admiration for someone whose skill or charm is enviable.\n\nFORMS:\n- {憎|にく}い (plain)\n- {憎|にく}くない (negative)\n- {憎|にく}かった (past)\n- {憎|にく}くて (te-form)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {憎|にく}くてたまらない: to hate unbearably\n- {憎|にく}いやつ: hateful person / impressive person (context-dependent)\n- {憎|にく}い{演出|えんしゅつ}: impressive staging\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {憎|にく}む: to hate (verb)\n- {憎|にく}しみ: hatred (noun)\n- {憎|にく}らしい: hateful, provoking (adjective, always negative)\n\nNOTE: Do not confuse with the suffix 〜にくい (difficult to do), which is a separate word.",
